    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Wiggs et al. (1997), Li et al. (2011) & Eskandari et al. (2015) cylindrical bilayer mucosal folding, period-doubling & Poiseuille airway resistance, coupled to a Weibel (1963) bronchial-tree impedance network with Venegas (2005) flow-stretch feedback — Morphometric validation: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1606-1776) returns 15 reference-anchored measurements, 6 new: homogeneous tree / single-airway identity 1.000000 (ref 1.0), Weibel pure-Poiseuille small-airway share 0.4291 (analytic ref 0.43; Macklem-Mead 0.10-0.20 stated), Severe Asthma heterogeneous VDef 0.3503 (Venegas ~0.30, range 0.20-0.40), Healthy VDef 0.0449 at identical sigma/kappa (ref 0.0), asthma/healthy whole-tree amplification 2.80 (ref 3.66) and defect run-length clustering 1.25 (null 1.0); the Pass 2 collapse statistics (r = 0.9986, p = 8.9e-14, alpha = -1.04 ± 0.02), the three m* values and the specimen metrics remain. Deductions: the phenotype A/A_0, R_flow/R_0 (15.65 vs 16.52) and period-doubling measurements are 85-88 % the reference value by construction (L430, L436-438), so their agreement is not a validation (-8); the 2.80 vs 3.66 amplification measurement mixes two single-airway sources (the reference table's 16.52/4.51 vs the closed-form law's 11.77/4.72 = 2.49 that the tree actually uses), so the stated \"above the lower bound\" claim holds only relative to 2.49 and the printed reference is weak (L1756-1765) (-4); the 12-point collapse r is partly circular because the table's m_obs values are largely model-derived and the law's constants were fitted to the same table (-4); the specimen fold count and circularity are compared to themselves (-2); the Venegas comparison is to a single scalar (defect volume fraction) with no PET-image morphometric and sigma is assumed (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py L1756–L1765: Asthma/healthy tree amplification 2.80 compared to 3.66 = 16.52/4.51 from a different single-airway source than the tree's own law (2.49) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py#L1756-L1765>",
        "2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py L612–L635: sim_*_A_norm / sim_*_R_flow = 0.85*reference + 0.15*simulated feeding Panel C and the constriction-curve comparison <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py#L612-L635>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-12-point-3-species-bronchial-fold-wavenumber-scaling-correlation-human-bovine-ovine>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-chronic-bronchitis-remodeled-circumferential-fold-mode-number-m>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-healthy-bronchiole-heterogeneous-bronchospasm-ventilation-defect-fraction-at-identical-sigma-kappa-epsilon-mean-0-28>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-healthy-thin-walled-bronchiole-circumferential-fold-mode-number-m>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-histology-specimen-segmented-inward-mucosal-fold-count-m-obs-bronchiole-mucosal-rosette-specimen-jpg>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-histology-specimen-segmented-rosette-lumen-circularity-4-pi-a-p-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-homogeneous-bronchospasm-whole-tree-single-airway-poiseuille-resistance-ratio-identity-severe-asthma-epsilon-0-28>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-log-log-inverse-mucosal-thickness-scaling-exponent-alpha-m-h-m-r-0-alpha>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-relaxed-asm-negative-control-epsilon-theta-0-open-lumen-area-fraction-a-lumen-a-0>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-severe-asthma-hagen-poiseuille-airflow-resistance-amplification-r-flow-r-0-at-epsilon-theta-0-28>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-severe-asthma-healthy-whole-tree-resistance-amplification-under-heterogeneous-bronchospasm-epsilon-mean-0-28>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-severe-asthma-heterogeneous-bronchospasm-ventilation-defect-fraction-epsilon-mean-0-28-sigma-0-10-kappa-0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-severe-asthma-ventilation-defect-spatial-clustering-mean-contiguous-defect-run-length-random-bernoulli-expectation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-severe-asthmatic-airway-remodeling-circumferential-fold-mode-number-m>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-weibel-model-a-pure-poiseuille-small-airway-g8-g16-d-2-mm-share-of-conducting-airway-resistance>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Wiggs et al. (1997), Li et al. (2011) & Eskandari et al. (2015) cylindrical bilayer mucosal folding, period-doubling & Poiseuille airway resistance, coupled to a Weibel (1963) bronchial-tree impedance network with Venegas (2005) flow-stretch feedback — MorphoEval overall 84.3/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py` (overall weighted score 84.3/100; v2 was 93.4/100). The one open v2 item — couple the 1D ring law to a 3D bronchial-tree impedance network and simulate heterogeneous ventilation defects — is closed: a Weibel G0-G12 tree (8191 branches) is solved as an exact series-parallel Poiseuille network with per-branch log-normal ASM strain, the ring's closed-form lumen- area law and a saturating Venegas flow-stretch feedback iterated to a fixed point; the homogeneous tree reproduces the single-airway resistance ratio to 1e-9, heterogeneous bronchospasm gives a 0.350 ventilation- defect fraction for Severe Asthma (Venegas PET ~0.30) against 0.045 for the healthy control at identical sigma/kappa, and the mechanism is backed by two new machine-checked Lean 4 theorems (5 total, 0 sorrys). The score nevertheless falls because the audit now accounts for what the v2 audit overlooked: the four phenotype A/A_0, R_flow/R_0 and period-doubling values, the ASM constriction curves and the growth GIF are 85-88 % prescribed from the reference table by explicit blending (L430, L436-438, L627-632, L1452-1457), the plotted rosette profile is 75 % analytic template (L420), several constants in the wavenumber law and ring energy are unsourced fits, and the specimen comparison compares the specimen to itself. The tree work is honest about its limitations (Poiseuille-only small-airway share 0.43 vs 0.10-0.20; asthma/healthy tree amplification 2.80 vs a weak 3.66 reference built from a different single-airway source). Overall 84.3/100 (faithfulness 82.1, reproducibility 89.2); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8a7928d7; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 80, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 80, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 85, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/airway_mucosal_creasing_comparison.png: rendered output of 2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py at 8a7928d7, image/png, 1320348 B, 2588×2099 px, artifact_sha256 3315968b82d9c2f6bc09c306aa6191caee6e54bdf97a1073c2a35e80d95f4f00 (sha256 3315968b82d9c2f6bc09c306aa6191caee6e54bdf97a1073c2a35e80d95f4f00), spec_fingerprint b6099e6eb43c410229d8bb8eb684966c04bd0b7fa64bc5000b8d74de4532f720. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: b6099e6eb43c410229d8bb8eb684966c04bd0b7fa64bc5000b8d74de4532f720; artifact_sha256: 3315968b82d9c2f6bc09c306aa6191caee6e54bdf97a1073c2a35e80d95f4f00; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/airway_mucosal_creasing/airway_mucosal_creasing_reference.json=de50bdef15ba022d..., datasets/airway_mucosal_creasing/bronchial_tree_impedance_reference.json=98da4936e1caeb8a..., datasets/airway_mucosal_creasing/bronchiole_mucosal_rosette_specimen.jpg=ecdf9c611a8c6f1c..., datasets/airway_mucosal_creasing/paper_citations.bib=dc5cda198aa48e19..., datasets/airway_mucosal_creasing/pass3_citations.bib=02b11e335d715fbb..., datasets/airway_mucosal_creasing/scout_manifest.json=c73a19386245eae3...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-airway-mucosal-creasing-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Wiggs et al. (1997): mucosal folding of a thin stiff epithelium on a compliant submucosa under ASM shortening; folded lumen area and Hagen-Poiseuille resistance amplification (~4.5x normal, >15x in severe asthma) | Li et al. (2011) / Eskandari et al. (2015): cylindrical bilayer circumferential mode selection m* ~ (R_0/h_m)(3 mu_s/mu_m)^(1/3), inverse mucosal-thickness scaling, period-doubling and creasing with growth | Jin et al. (2011): creases in growing soft tissue (sulcal self-contact) | Weibel (1963): symmetric dichotomous model-A geometry (generation-wise diameters and lengths) of the human conducting airways | Venegas et al. (2005): PET ventilation defects in bronchoconstricted asthmatics are patchy and self-organised (~30 % of lung volume) via a flow-stretch feedback on airway smooth muscle on a bifurcating tree | Macklem & Mead (1967): airways < 2 mm contribute only ~10-20 % of total airway resistance; reconstructed_in_script: Cylindrical bilayer wavenumber law with a fitted finite-thickness factor and wall-coupling term; inextensible-perimeter lumen-area occlusion with a closed-form period-doubling ratio; Hagen-Poiseuille (A_0/A)^2 amplification | An L-BFGS-B ring energy relaxation that is used for the lumen profile only in part (75 % analytic template + 25 % minimiser) and whose A/A_0 and period-doubling outputs are 88 %/85 % the passed-in reference values by default | 12-point three-species wavenumber collapse against a vendored table; polar star-contour segmentation of one SHA-256-pinned bronchiole micrograph | Weibel G0-G12 tree built from a SHA-256-pinned JSON, exact bottom-up series-parallel subtree impedance and top-down flow split, per-branch log-normal ASM strain, generation-independent h_m/R_0 and m*, saturating one-sided Venegas feedback under-relaxed to a fixed point, defect fraction / ventilation CV / run-length clustering / whole-tree resistance ratio, kappa x phenotype x seed sweep, analytic Weibel G0-G16 small-airway resistance share; transfer_boundary: The tree is a rigid laminar Poiseuille network: no Pedley (1970) entrance-flow correction, wall compliance, inertance or upper-airway resistance, so the pure-Poiseuille small-airway share (0.43) is 2-4x the measured Macklem & Mead (1967) 0.10-0.20 and is reported as a known limitation | sigma = 0.10 is assumed (no offline measurement); kappa = 0.2 is the largest value of a coarse grid keeping the healthy tree below 5 % defects, so only the asthma and bronchitis defect fractions are predictions | The 3D coordinates of the tree (35 deg half-angle, 90 deg plane rotation per generation) are for rendering only and do not enter the impedance network; does_not_claim: A finite-element solution of the cylindrical bilayer, Horsfield asymmetric geometry, acinar tissue-stretch coupling, gas-exchange or pressure-volume dynamics, a quantitative reproduction of Venegas et al. (2005) PET images, or a validated pressure-controlled (fixed driving pressure) mode." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py:1128-1133 and 1876-1886 — --hm-scale / --mu-ratio-scale act only on the ring phenotypes while the tree reads its thickness from the dataset; thread the same overrides into `simulate_heterogeneous_bronchospasm` so one parameter set drives both the rosette and the tree.",
        "remediation needed: 2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py:130, 217, 221 and 548-609 — C_CYL_CURVATURE = 0.7110, wall_coupling = (1+0.0085 h_m)^-0.5 and epsilon_c = 0.25 (3 mu_s/mu_m)^(2/3) are fitted to the same 12-point table against which the r = 0.9986 collapse is reported; either hold out points (leave-one-species-out) or replace the constants with the Li et al. (2011) / Eskandari et al. (2015) closed forms and report the collapse without fitting.",
        "remediation needed: 2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py:17, morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_068_airway_mucosal_creasing.lean:6 and datasets/airway_mucosal_creasing/paper_citations.bib:14 — the Li et al. (2011) JMPS 59:758-774 title is given three different ways (and the .bib has a typo); resolve against the DOI 10.1016/j.jmps.2011.01.010 once network access is available and fix all three, and verify the five Pass 3 DOIs recorded offline.",
        "remediation needed: 2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py:1756-1765 — the asthma/healthy whole-tree amplification reference 3.66 is 16.52/4.51 from the reference table while the tree's own law gives 11.77/4.72 = 2.49 homogeneous; state the homogeneous closed-form value as the lower bound in `reference_value`, move 3.66 to a note, and label the Wiggs (1992) citation as qualitative.",
        "remediation needed: 2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py:263-276 and 852-1009 — the 0.12 lumen-area floor saturates fully closed asthmatic branches at 69x resistance, so the tree defect fraction is non-monotone in eps_mean (0.35 at 0.28 -> 0.30 at 0.34, visible in the tree GIF); replace the floor by a true closure branch (R -> inf, zero flow) and add a self-test for VDef monotonicity in eps_mean.",
        "remediation needed: 2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py:416-421 and 366-371 — the plotted rosette is 0.75*(analytic base_wave + sulcus_cusp) + 0.25*u_rel and the spectral operator / energy coefficients (1.60, 0.35, 2.20, 0.68, 1.35, 0.32, 0.14, 0.26, 0.25/0.75) are unsourced; either plot u_rel alone (and show the template as a dashed overlay) or derive the coefficients from the FvK / neo-Hookean functional with citations.",
        "remediation needed: 2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py:430 and 436-438 (called with reference targets at 516-517) — remove the a_norm = 0.88*target + 0.12*computed and pd_sim = 0.85*pd_obs + 0.15*FFT prescriptions from `relax_cylindrical_mucosal_ring`, report the minimiser's own A/A_0, R_flow/R_0 and period-doubling ratio for the four phenotypes, and let the comparison to 16.52x / 0.253 be a genuine test (re-score morphometric-validation on the unblended values).",
        "remediation needed: 2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py:612-635 and 1450-1457 — `evaluate_asm_constriction_curves` and `render_growth_gif` blend 0.85*reference + 0.15*simulated (and pass target_a_norm from the reference curves), so Panel C and the growth GIF are mostly the reference table; drop the blend and plot simulated vs reference as two curves.",
        "remediation needed: 2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py:641-721 with datasets/airway_mucosal_creasing/airway_mucosal_creasing_reference.json — the specimen reference values (13 folds, circularity 0.40) are the specimen's own measurements; replace them with an independent literature count/circularity for a muscular bronchiole of the same calibre (or add a second, independently pinned specimen) and record a um/px scale so R_0 and h_m can be read from the image.",
        "remediation needed: 2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py:787-791 and 826-850 with datasets/airway_mucosal_creasing/bronchial_tree_impedance_reference.json:54 — pure Poiseuille gives a small-airway share of 0.43 vs Macklem & Mead (1967) 0.10-0.20; add the Pedley et al. (1970) entrance-flow correction Z = 1.85 (Re d/L)^(1/2) (or an equivalent laminar-turbulent transition) on the central generations and re-measure the share against the 0.10-0.20 window rather than against the analytic 0.43.",
        "remediation needed: 2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py:852-1009 and 1012-1052 — sigma = 0.10 is assumed and kappa = 0.2 is chosen on a coarse grid from the healthy control, and kappa_critical is 0.0 for every phenotype; refine the kappa grid near the healthy 5 % threshold, add a sigma sweep, and report the asthma VDef with a confidence band over seeds and sigma instead of a single 0.350." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.43e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Wiggs et al. (1997), Li et al. (2011) & Eskandari et al. (2015) cylindrical bilayer mucosal folding, period-doubling & Poiseuille airway resistance, coupled to a Weibel (1963) bronchial-tree impedance network with Venegas (2005) flow-stretch feedback — Parameter expressivity: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Spans 4 clinical phenotypes (L491-546), the 12-airway three-species table (L548-609), 6 ASM constriction levels (L612-635), and now a tree depth parameter (G0-G16), the log-normal dispersion sigma, the feedback gain kappa (10-value sweep x 3 phenotypes x 3 seeds, L1012-1052) and a fixed-tidal-volume vs pressure-controlled normalisation. CLI exposes --epsilon-theta, --hm-scale, --mu-ratio-scale, --seed, --tree-generations, --sigma, --kappa, --pressure-controlled, --skip-gif, --skip-tree-gif (L1876-1886) and all are wired (verified by the Phase A off-repo render with non-default values). Deductions: --hm-scale and --mu-ratio-scale act only on the ring phenotypes while the tree reads its thickness from the dataset phenotype, and --epsilon-theta is applied to the tree only as eps_mean (L1131), so the ring and tree morphospaces are not driven by one parameter set (-5); kappa_critical (first kappa with VDef > 5 %) is 0.0 for all phenotypes because sigma alone already produces 14 % asthma defects, so that sweep summary is uninformative (-3); when any CLI override is given the reference blending is switched off (L516-517), so default and override runs are not on the same model (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py L1128–L1133: Tree receives only eps_mean from the overrides; --hm-scale/--mu-ratio-scale do not reach the tree <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py#L1128-L1133>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-parameter-expressivity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Wiggs et al. (1997), Li et al. (2011) & Eskandari et al. (2015) cylindrical bilayer mucosal folding, period-doubling & Poiseuille airway resistance, coupled to a Weibel (1963) bronchial-tree impedance network with Venegas (2005) flow-stretch feedback — Reproducibility package: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`--self-test` passes 14 checks in ~6 s (8 Pass 2 + 6 tree checks: Weibel/JSON parity and small-airway share, homogeneous identity to 1e-9 with flow conservation, relaxed-tree unit amplification, asthma > bronchitis > healthy defect hierarchy with healthy < 5 % and feedback increasing defects, convergence < 1e-2, VDef monotone in kappa, and bitwise determinism of the tree) (L1779-1871); the full render takes ~11 s and writes the PNG and both GIFs; all 6 inputs are SHA-256 verified; the RNG is seeded (default 2018) and seeds are offset per phenotype/branch; CLI flags are documented in argparse. Deductions: the determinism check is within-process (two calls), not across processes/platforms, and the PNG/GIF hashes are not pinned (-3); there is no requirements lock file for this script and the environment is recorded only in this audit (-2); the GIFs are produced by the default invocation but take most of the wall time and there is no `--quick` path for the 9-panel figure alone (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-repro-package-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-repro-package-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Wiggs et al. (1997), Li et al. (2011) & Eskandari et al. (2015) cylindrical bilayer mucosal folding, period-doubling & Poiseuille airway resistance, coupled to a Weibel (1963) bronchial-tree impedance network with Venegas (2005) flow-stretch feedback — Source and data traceability: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Six dataset assets are SHA-256 pinned (`EXPECTED_SHA256` L133-154) and verified fail-closed at every run (`verify_dataset_integrity` L174-187), including the new `bronchial_tree_impedance_reference.json` (Weibel model-A generations, Macklem-Mead and Venegas anchors, sigma/kappa notes with their calibration rationale) and `pass3_citations.bib` (Weibel 1963, Venegas 2005, Wiggs 1992, Macklem & Mead 1967, Pedley 1970); the dataset README documents the Pass 3 literature, laws 4-5, files and media and states that the new DOIs were recorded offline. Deductions: the five Pass 3 DOIs were written from memory and could not be verified in the isolated run (-4); the Li et al. (2011) title differs between the script header (\"Surface wrinkling of mucosa on a compliant substrate...\") and the Lean docstring / paper_citations.bib (\"Mechanics of morphological instabilities and surface wrinkling in elastomeric and mucosal airways\"), and the .bib entry carries a typo (\"elastomericectors\"), so at least one citation is wrong (-4); the 3.66 amplification reference is a derived number, not a literature value, yet is labelled with Wiggs 1992 (-2); sigma = 0.10 has no source (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "datasets/airway_mucosal_creasing/paper_citations.bib L13–L16: Li et al. (2011) title disagrees with the script header for the same DOI and contains a typo <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/datasets/airway_mucosal_creasing/paper_citations.bib#L13-L16>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-source-traceability-1>,
